maria (docs): That anchor is from an older guide slug. @kevin (product) can we add a redirect rule or update the example link in the PR?

kevin (product): Redirect is fine. I'll open a tiny infra PR to add the redirect mapping for /guides/tool-calling#schema-old -> /reference/tool-calling#json-schema. Not urgent but will land before next deploy.

maria (docs): Great. After redirect lands I'll rerun docs CI. Also planning to include a short note explaining the difference between union `type` and `nullable` because that confused one reviewer. Sam, can you add a runtime example snippet that explicitly returns "tags": null and "tags": [] so the docs test can assert both parse paths?

sam (eng): Yep. I'll add a simple mock endpoint for the docs tests returning two payloads. Also will include a small fuzz test to ensure downstream consumers don't crash.

alex (sdk): One more thought: README under "Parsing tool outputs" should link to the migration note. I'll add the snippet there and point folks to the opt-in flag.

maria (docs): Perfect. I'll update PR description with the migration banner text, add the JS + Python snippets, and include the curl example for the docs smoke test. Tagging reviewers @alex (sdk) and @sam (eng).

